\import{macros}
\meta{agent-authored}{true}

\taxon{Remark}
\title{Where compute is spent}
\tag{ftip}
\tag{compute}

\p{Post-training consumes compute at several distinct interfaces. A policy
generates a rollout. An environment executes actions, and a verifier checks
evidence. The optimizer then transforms feedback into a parameter update.
Evaluation and deployment consume additional inference compute.}

\p{These operations cannot be counted by one unqualified number of steps.
Reusing a rollout can reduce generation while increasing update work.
Predicting a later checkpoint can reduce realized optimizer steps while adding
checkpoint, fitting, and recovery costs. \citef{miao2026when} and
\citef{chen2026lowrank} study these two interventions in particular settings.}

\p{FTIP will therefore record a typed cost vector before asking for an optimum.
This remark introduces no cost formula. It states the accounting requirement
that later definitions must satisfy.}
